# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use gates and readout instructions on IBM QPUs that are calibrated differently from the default set, such as slow gates and shorter measurements"
msgstr "Gumamit ng mga gate at readout instruction sa mga IBM QPU na iba ang pagkaka-calibrate kumpara sa default na set, tulad ng mga mabagal na gate at mas maiikling measurement"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specially calibrated instructions"
msgstr "Mga espesyal na na-calibrate na instruction"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specially calibrated instructions {#specially-calibrated-instructions}"
msgstr "Mga espesyal na na-calibrate na instruction {#specially-calibrated-instructions}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default, the quantum gates and readout operations on IBM&reg; quantum computers are calibrated for optimal performance across general use cases. Some workloads, however, benefit from instructions whose parameters are tuned differently. For example, [`MidCircuitMeasure`](/guides/execute-dynamic-circuits#midcircuitmeasure-method) (`measure_2`) is a readout operation tailored for measurements in the middle of a circuit, and slower `cz` gates can improve the results of some error mitigation workflows.\n"
msgstr "Bilang default, ang mga quantum gate at readout operation sa mga quantum computer ng IBM&reg; ay naka-calibrate para sa pinakamainam na performance sa mga pangkalahatang use case. Pero may mga workload na mas nakikinabang sa mga instruction na iba ang pagkaka-tune ng mga parameter. Halimbawa, ang [`MidCircuitMeasure`](/guides/execute-dynamic-circuits#midcircuitmeasure-method) (`measure_2`) ay isang readout operation na ginawa para sa mga measurement sa gitna ng circuit, at ang mas mabagal na mga `cz` gate ay makakapagpabuti sa resulta ng ilang error mitigation workflow.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specially calibrated instructions come in two forms, and you access them differently:\n"
msgstr "Dalawa ang anyo ng mga espesyal na na-calibrate na instruction, at magkaiba ang paraan ng pag-access sa mga ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[**Instructions with different signatures**](#different) are calibrated alongside the standard instructions in the default calibration, so you add them to your circuits like any other instruction. They are usually identified by a suffix, such as `measure_2`.\n"
msgstr "[**Mga instruction na may magkakaibang signature**](#different) ay kina-calibrate kasabay ng mga standard na instruction sa default calibration, kaya idinadagdag mo ang mga ito sa iyong mga circuit tulad ng ibang instruction. Karaniwan silang natutukoy sa pamamagitan ng suffix, tulad ng `measure_2`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[**Alternative calibrations**](#alternative-calibrations) replace parts of the default calibration with differently tuned parameters. You select one by passing a `calibration_id` when you retrieve the backend.\n"
msgstr "[**Mga alternatibong calibration**](#alternative-calibrations) ay pumapalit sa ilang bahagi ng default calibration gamit ang mga parameter na iba ang pagkaka-tune. Pipili ka ng isa sa pamamagitan ng pagpasa ng `calibration_id` kapag kinuha mo ang backend.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To learn how IBM quantum computers are calibrated, see [Monitor, calibrate, and benchmark](/guides/calibration-jobs).\n"
msgstr "Para malaman kung paano kina-calibrate ang mga IBM quantum computer, tingnan ang [Mag-monitor, mag-calibrate, at mag-benchmark](/guides/calibration-jobs).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"different\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instructions with different signatures {#instructions-with-different-signatures}"
msgstr "Mga instruction na may magkakaibang signature {#instructions-with-different-signatures}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These instructions are calibrated with the standard instruction set, so you don't need to do anything special to retrieve a backend that supports them. To use one, add the corresponding `qiskit-ibm-runtime` instruction to your circuit.\n"
msgstr "Kina-calibrate ang mga instruction na ito kasama ng standard instruction set, kaya wala kang kailangang gawing espesyal para makakuha ng backend na sumusuporta sa mga ito. Para gumamit ng isa, idagdag ang katumbas na `qiskit-ibm-runtime` instruction sa iyong circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Instruction | Description | Typical use case | Use in Qiskit | Processor family |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| `measure_2` | Shorter measurement pulse | [Mid-circuit measurements](/guides/execute-dynamic-circuits#midcircuitmeasure-method) | [`MidCircuitMeasure`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/circuit-library-mid-circuit-measure) (v0.43.0 or later) | Heron, Nighthawk r2 |\n"
"| `reset_2` | Shorter conditional reset pulse that uses `measure_2` | Mid-circuit qubit reset | [`MidCircuitReset`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/circuit-library-mid-circuit-reset) (v0.49.0 or later) | Heron |\n"
"| `measure_reset` | Measurement like `measure` that also resets the qubit* | Measure and reset a qubit | [`MeasureReset`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/circuit-library-measure-reset) (v0.50.0 or later) | Heron, Nighthawk r2 |\n"
"| `measure_reset_2` | Shorter measurement like `measure_2` that also resets the qubit* | Measure and reset a qubit mid-circuit | Initialize [`MeasureReset`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/circuit-library-measure-reset) with `name=\"measure_reset_2\"` (v0.50.0 or later) | Heron, Nighthawk r2 |\n"
"| `xslow` | Bit-flip (X) gate with an extended duration | [Postselection](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation/guides/postselection-with-non-markovian-error-checks) and error mitigation. It is the default value of the `x_pulse_type` option in [postselection passes](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-mitigation/postselection-passes) | All |\n"
". | [`XSlowGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/circuit-library-x-slow-gate#xslowgate) (v0.50.0 or later) | All |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Instruction | Paglalarawan | Karaniwang use case | Paggamit sa Qiskit | Processor family |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| `measure_2` | Mas maikling measurement pulse | [Mga mid-circuit measurement](/guides/execute-dynamic-circuits#midcircuitmeasure-method) | [`MidCircuitMeasure`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/circuit-library-mid-circuit-measure) (v0.43.0 o mas bago) | Heron, Nighthawk r2 |\n"
"| `reset_2` | Mas maikling conditional reset pulse na gumagamit ng `measure_2` | Mid-circuit qubit reset | [`MidCircuitReset`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/circuit-library-mid-circuit-reset) (v0.49.0 o mas bago) | Heron |\n"
"| `measure_reset` | Measurement na tulad ng `measure` na nagre-reset din ng qubit* | Mag-measure at mag-reset ng qubit | [`MeasureReset`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/circuit-library-measure-reset) (v0.50.0 o mas bago) | Heron, Nighthawk r2 |\n"
"| `measure_reset_2` | Mas maikling measurement na tulad ng `measure_2` na nagre-reset din ng qubit* | Mag-measure at mag-reset ng qubit sa gitna ng circuit | I-initialize ang [`MeasureReset`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/circuit-library-measure-reset) gamit ang `name=\"measure_reset_2\"` (v0.50.0 o mas bago) | Heron, Nighthawk r2 |\n"
"| `xslow` | Bit-flip (X) gate na may pinahabang duration | [Postselection](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation/guides/postselection-with-non-markovian-error-checks) at error mitigation. Ito ang default na value ng option na `x_pulse_type` sa [mga postselection pass](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-mitigation/postselection-passes) | Lahat |\n"
". | [`XSlowGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/circuit-library-x-slow-gate#xslowgate) (v0.50.0 o mas bago) | Lahat |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\* On Heron processors, the reset is conditional on the measurement result. On Nighthawk r2 processors, the reset is unconditional.\n"
msgstr "\\* Sa mga Heron processor, nakadepende sa resulta ng measurement ang reset. Sa mga Nighthawk r2 processor, unconditional ang reset.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because these instructions are not supported on every backend, check the backend's supported instructions before you use them:\n"
msgstr "Dahil hindi sinusuportahan ang mga instruction na ito sa bawat backend, tingnan muna ang mga sinusuportahang instruction ng backend bago mo gamitin ang mga ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To find all backends that support an instruction, use:\n"
msgstr "Para mahanap ang lahat ng backend na sumusuporta sa isang instruction, gamitin ang:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use `instruction_signatures` to see the signatures of these specially calibrated instructions:\n"
msgstr "Gamitin ang `instruction_signatures` para makita ang mga signature ng mga espesyal na na-calibrate na instruction na ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alternative calibrations {#alternative-calibrations}"
msgstr "Mga alternatibong calibration {#alternative-calibrations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alternative calibrations replace parts of the default calibration with differently tuned parameters. Each alternative calibration has a calibration ID, and its availability depends on the QPU.\n"
msgstr "Pinapalitan ng mga alternatibong calibration ang ilang bahagi ng default calibration gamit ang mga parameter na iba ang pagkaka-tune. Bawat alternatibong calibration ay may calibration ID, at nakadepende sa QPU ang availability nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To use an alternative calibration, pass its `calibration_id` when you retrieve the backend. The backend's target, and therefore the transpiler, uses the instruction properties from that calibration, and primitive jobs that you run on the backend execute with it.\n"
msgstr "Para gumamit ng alternatibong calibration, ipasa ang `calibration_id` nito kapag kinuha mo ang backend. Ginagamit ng target ng backend, at kaya ng transpiler, ang mga instruction property mula sa calibration na iyon, at ang mga primitive job na pinapatakbo mo sa backend ay isinasagawa gamit ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Alternative calibrations are not available on all QPUs.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Hindi available ang mga alternatibong calibration sa lahat ng QPU.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Slow gate calibrations {#slow-gate-calibrations}"
msgstr "Mga slow gate calibration {#slow-gate-calibrations}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Slow gate calibrations tune the `cz` gate to be slower than in the default calibration. Slower `cz` gates might improve performance for large-scale observable estimation workflows with error mitigation, but they also increase the total duration of your circuit, which causes some additional decoherence.\n"
msgstr "Ina-tune ng mga slow gate calibration ang `cz` gate para maging mas mabagal kaysa sa default calibration. Posibleng mapabuti ng mas mabagal na mga `cz` gate ang performance para sa malakihang observable estimation workflow na may error mitigation, pero pinahahaba rin nito ang kabuuang duration ng iyong circuit, na nagdudulot ng kaunting karagdagang decoherence.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On Heron processors, slow gate calibrations are also available with two modes of two-level system (TLS) bias control:\n"
msgstr "Sa mga Heron processor, available din ang mga slow gate calibration na may dalawang mode ng two-level system (TLS) bias control:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**DC TLS bias** is optimized for the best instantaneous performance. The default calibration uses DC TLS bias.\n"
msgstr "Ang **DC TLS bias** ay naka-optimize para sa pinakamahusay na instantaneous performance. Gumagamit ng DC TLS bias ang default calibration.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**AC TLS bias** modulates the TLS bias to stabilize device errors over time, which keeps the device's noise model stable during lengthy workflows. See \"Noise stabilization\" in [Observable Estimation in the Absence of Classical Verification](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2607.25998#page=52) for details.\n"
msgstr "Ang **AC TLS bias** ay minomodulate ang TLS bias para i-stabilize ang mga error ng device sa paglipas ng panahon, na nagpapanatiling stable ng noise model ng device sa mahahabang workflow. Tingnan ang \"Noise stabilization\" sa [Observable Estimation in the Absence of Classical Verification](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2607.25998#page=52) para sa mga detalye.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nighthawk processors do not use TLS bias, so they have a single slow gate calibration.\n"
msgstr "Hindi gumagamit ng TLS bias ang mga Nighthawk processor, kaya iisa lang ang slow gate calibration nila.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Calibration ID | Processor family | TLS bias | Recommended for |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| None (default calibration) | All | DC (Heron) | General use. Especially recommended for workloads whose bitstrings can be classically distilled, such as peaked circuits and [SQD or SKQD](/learning/courses/integrating-quantum-and-high-performance-computing/sqd-skqd) workflows, and for workloads with [error detection](/tutorials/spacetime-codes). |\n"
"| `slow_gates_dc` | Heron | DC | Large-scale observable estimation workflows, especially those that use heuristic error mitigation such as zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE). |\n"
"| `slow_gates_ac` | Heron | AC | Workflows that require stable error rates over long sessions. Strongly recommended for workflows that involve noise learning, such as probabilistic error amplification (PEA) and probabilistic error cancellation (PEC). |\n"
"| `slow_gates` | Nighthawk | Not applicable | Observable estimation workflows that use error mitigation, such as ZNE, PEA, and PEC. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Calibration ID | Processor family | TLS bias | Inirerekomenda para sa |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| Wala (default calibration) | Lahat | DC (Heron) | Pangkalahatang gamit. Lalo na inirerekomenda para sa mga workload na ang mga bitstring ay maaaring i-distill nang classical, tulad ng mga peaked circuit at [SQD o SKQD](/learning/courses/integrating-quantum-and-high-performance-computing/sqd-skqd) workflow, at para sa mga workload na may [error detection](/tutorials/spacetime-codes). |\n"
"| `slow_gates_dc` | Heron | DC | Malakihang observable estimation workflow, lalo na ang mga gumagamit ng heuristic error mitigation tulad ng zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE). |\n"
"| `slow_gates_ac` | Heron | AC | Mga workflow na nangangailangan ng stable na error rate sa mahahabang session. Mariing inirerekomenda para sa mga workflow na may noise learning, tulad ng probabilistic error amplification (PEA) at probabilistic error cancellation (PEC). |\n"
"| `slow_gates` | Nighthawk | Hindi naaangkop | Mga observable estimation workflow na gumagamit ng error mitigation, tulad ng ZNE, PEA, at PEC. |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example:\n"
msgstr "Halimbawa:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"When you use `slow_gates_ac`, submit all jobs in the workflow to a single [session](/guides/run-jobs-session) so that they run while the device's noise remains stable.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"Kapag ginamit mo ang `slow_gates_ac`, isumite ang lahat ng job sa workflow sa iisang [session](/guides/run-jobs-session) para tumakbo ang mga ito habang stable pa ang noise ng device.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check gate durations {#check-gate-durations}"
msgstr "Suriin ang mga gate duration {#check-gate-durations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because slow gate calibrations increase `cz` gate durations, compare the durations against the default calibration to understand the effect on your circuit. Use the backend's target to find the duration, in seconds, of the `cz` gate on a specific pair of qubits:\n"
msgstr "Dahil pinahahaba ng mga slow gate calibration ang duration ng `cz` gate, ihambing ang mga duration sa default calibration para maunawaan ang epekto sa iyong circuit. Gamitin ang target ng backend para hanapin ang duration, sa segundo, ng `cz` gate sa isang partikular na pares ng mga qubit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the target reflects the selected calibration, transpile your circuits against the backend that uses the same `calibration_id` you plan to run on.\n"
msgstr "Dahil sinasalamin ng target ang napiling calibration, i-transpile ang iyong mga circuit laban sa backend na gumagamit ng parehong `calibration_id` na balak mong patakbuhin.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Mga susunod na hakbang {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- Learn how to [execute dynamic circuits](/guides/execute-dynamic-circuits) with mid-circuit measurements.\n"
"- Use [postselection](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation/guides/postselection-with-non-markovian-error-checks) to filter out results affected by correlated noise.\n"
"- Read about how IBM quantum computers are [monitored, calibrated, and benchmarked](/guides/calibration-jobs).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Mga rekomendasyon\">\n"
"- Alamin kung paano [magpatakbo ng mga dynamic circuit](/guides/execute-dynamic-circuits) na may mid-circuit measurement.\n"
"- Gamitin ang [postselection](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation/guides/postselection-with-non-markovian-error-checks) para i-filter out ang mga resultang naapektuhan ng correlated noise.\n"
"- Basahin kung paano [minomonitor, kina-calibrate, at bina-benchmark](/guides/calibration-jobs) ang mga IBM quantum computer.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
